also averages 1.046 × forecast, so ordering slightly above forecast pays.\n\nCandidate 7 orders below the others and runs short more often. Candidate 5 orders 1–2 units more each time. But it under-covers the demand spike: 52 of item 1 against about 60 expected for days 19–20, and 72 of item 0 against about 78. Overall it comes out roughly even with candidate 2.\n\n**3. Candidate 2 vs 4.** These two plans are identical through day 22.\n- Candidate 4 covers item 0 for days 27–29 with one order: 58 units on day 24.\n- Candidate 2 splits it into 44 units on day 24 and 20 on day 26. That costs an extra 39 order fee plus 6 more units (54).\n- It gains only about 2 more units sold (≈ 35 including the avoided penalty).\n- On item 1 the two plans come out about even.\n\nSo candidate 4 is ahead by about 55. Candidate 5 ends the same way as candidate 2, so it loses that difference too.\n\n**Capacity and spoilage.** In the every-2-days plans, the busiest day (day 19) peaks at about 143 of the 160 units of space. Stock is cleared within its shelf life, so spoilage losses are small."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3942, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3942}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T02:14:03.276Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAnaTqaA2aqqjsyT41hG"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Fh5tSPdxs3S3zRDWhoYcwa", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_to